	c := getCommand(ExactArgs(2), false)
	_, err := executeCommand(c, "a", "b", "c")
	exactArgsWithInvalidCount(err, t)
}
```
Concrete counts: `ExactArgs(2)` is configured, and the command is run with 3 arguments (`a b c`).

The shared assertion helper (`args_test.go:88-97`) requires a non-nil error whose message is exactly `accepts 2 arg(s), received 3`.

